{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Split out of chewed-illicit-blacklemur (b8f7-65be-ec00-4844). Distinct defect, distinct fix.\n\nTEST: tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py::test_plan_review_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union\n(and its two siblings, test_code_review_* / test_completion_*, which share the same helper).\n\nSIGNATURE: AssertionError: clones do not share a base\n\n## Confirmed root cause\n\nThe failing assertion is a FIXTURE PRECONDITION, not the I1 append-only invariant under test.\nIn `_assert_emit_is_append_only`, clone A pushes its padded sidecar base to origin/tickets and\nclone B is then expected to hold the same base. B's sync is driven only as an incidental side\neffect of a read:\n\n    _git(\"push\", \"-q\", \"origin\", \"HEAD:tickets\", cwd=tracker_a)\n    _expire_sync_marker(tracker_b)\n    _engine_run(repo_b, \"list\")          # <- the only thing that syncs B\n    ...\n    assert base_a == _sidecar_paths(tracker_b, ...), \"clones do not share a base\"\n\nThat read-freshness path is best-effort BY DESIGN. `rebar._engine_support.reads.ensure_fresh`\nis throttled by a /tmp marker, calls `reconverge` with a deliberately SHORT lock timeout, and\nswallows every failure (\"a read must never fail because a fetch could not run\"). So `list`\nreturns 0 whether or not B pulled A's push. Under CI load (contended lock / slow runner) the\nreconverge is skipped or times out silently, B keeps its stale base, and the test fails while\nbuilding its own setup. The append-only behaviour the test exists to prove is never reached,\nso the red is a false alarm that costs a Verified -1.\n\nReproduced deterministically on this checkout by forcing the incidental sync to be a no-op\n(`REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off`, which `ensure_fresh` honours): all three two-clone-union tests fail\nwith exactly `AssertionError: clones do not share a base`. With the sync left enabled they\npass. That isolates the precondition to the best-effort side effect and rules out a product\ndefect in sidecar emit.\n\n## Fix\n\nMake the fixture ASSERT its precondition instead of relying on a side effect:\n\n1. Add a `_sync_from_origin(tracker)` helper that fetches `origin tickets` and fast-forwards\n   the tracker onto `FETCH_HEAD`, both with `check=True`, so a sync failure raises at its own\n   call site as a setup error rather than surfacing later as a misleading invariant failure.\n2. Replace `_expire_sync_marker(tracker_b)` + `_engine_run(repo_b, \"list\")` in\n   `_assert_emit_is_append_only` with that explicit call.\n3. Label the two setup assertions distinctly from the I1 invariant assertions so triage can\n   tell a setup failure from a real append-only violation.\n4. Document at the helper why the production read path must NOT be used to establish a\n   fixture precondition.\n\nDeterministic sync, not a retry loop. Content/ordering assertions only - no wall-clock or\ntiming-budget assertions are added.\n\nScope: tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py only. No production code changes; the\nproduct behaviour under test is unchanged and still fully exercised.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `_assert_emit_is_append_only` establishes clone B's shared base with an explicit\n      checked `git fetch` + `git merge --ff-only`; it no longer calls `_engine_run(repo_b,\n      \"list\")` or `_expire_sync_marker` to make the base converge.\n- [ ] AC2: The two shared-base preconditions are asserted with messages that identify them as\n      SETUP failures, textually distinct from the I1 append-only invariant messages.\n- [ ] AC3: With the incidental read-sync disabled (`REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off`) all three\n      `*_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union` tests PASS on the fixed code; on the pre-fix code the\n      same command fails all three with `AssertionError: clones do not share a base`.\n- [ ] AC4: All three tests pass under the default environment, and the file adds no wall-clock\n      or timing-budget assertion (assertions remain content/ordering facts).\n- [ ] AC5: `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786527807402538001,"uuid":"6cd860fa-5128-4824-bb2d-b8013a099407"}